('rifts', 'gr_damage_per_level_high', 1.02337, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 3: monster damage times this per level above gr_damage_mid_last_level, up to the Greater Rift cap. greater_rifts.csv monster_damage_scaling_per_rank'),
('rifts', 'gr_damage_per_level_low', 1.13185, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 3: monster damage times this per level, for levels 2 up to gr_damage_low_last_level. greater_rifts.csv monster_damage_scaling_per_rank (maxroll, ruling 2026-09-12)'),
('rifts', 'gr_damage_per_level_mid', 1.07177, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 3: monster damage times this per level, for levels above gr_damage_low_last_level up to gr_damage_mid_last_level. greater_rifts.csv monster_damage_scaling_per_rank'),
('rifts', 'gr_gold_per_level', 1.0103, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): Guardian gold times this per Greater Rift level above 1. greater_rifts.csv gold_gain_per_rank says +1.03% per rank, multiplicative (maxroll.gg/d3/resources/greater-rifts, pasted by ruling 2026-09-12). The same sheet''s gold_reward_scaling row reads +3% flat per rank from rank 26, which this does not apply: set 1.03 here if x1.03 was meant'),
('rifts', 'gr_guardian_xp_multiple', NULL, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 7, XP split: how many times its normal kill XP the Guardian of a Greater Rift gives (1 = unchanged). ALEX SETS IT: greater_rifts.csv other_rules says the Guardian awards a large amount and publishes no number (monster_xp.csv boss_xp_multiplier: NOT PUBLISHED). Blank leaves its XP as it is'),
('rifts', 'gr_legendary_bend', NULL, 1.05, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): curve A''s exponent, legendaries = start + (cap - start) x ((level - 1) / (cap level - 1)) ^ this below the cap level'),
('rifts', 'gr_legendary_cap', NULL, 12.0, 'count', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): legendaries a Guardian drops at the cap level and above (card 6b: 12; measured D3 on one player, 180 drops)'),
('rifts', 'gr_legendary_cap_level', NULL, 90.0, 'level', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): the Greater Rift level from which a Guardian drops the cap number of legendaries (card 6b: 12 at GR 90, flat after)'),
('rifts', 'gr_legendary_start', NULL, 0.04, 'count', 'Greater Rift part 8 (diablocraft-yxsa; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 8, docs/proposals/greater-rifts.md card 6b, ruling 2026-10-04): legendaries a level 1 Greater Rift Guardian drops on average, curve A''s start. The brief''s own derivation: the general legendary rate (loot_tuning.csv elite row, 1%) times the Guardian''s item count (the rift_guardian row''s 3 to 5 drops, 4 on average) = 0.04. The fraction is the chance of one more; there is no guaranteed legendary'),
('rifts', 'gr_level_one_tier', NULL, 2.0, 'count', 'Greater Rift part 3 (diablocraft-5o8y): the tier id whose Life and damage a Greater Rift level 1 monster has, the base the per-level factors multiply. 2 = Hard (dc_tier_phase), greater_rifts.csv equivalent_tier_gr1: GR 1 plays like Hard (the designer, read from the Diablo III client 2026-09-12). With this base GR 10 and GR 25 land within 1% of Torment I and VI on Life and damage; a Normal base would be a factor 2 short'),
('rifts', 'gr_life_per_level', 1.17, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 3: monster Life times this per Greater Rift level above 1. greater_rifts.csv monster_health_scaling_per_rank and monster_health_scaling_bands (maxroll.gg/d3/resources/greater-rifts, pasted by ruling 2026-09-12)'),
('rifts', 'gr_monster_xp_pct', NULL, NULL, 'percent', 'Greater Rift part 7, XP split: the percent of its normal kill XP a monster other than the Guardian gives inside a Greater Rift (100 = unchanged). ALEX SETS IT: greater_rifts.csv other_rules says monsters award less XP and publishes no number (monster_xp.csv: NOT PUBLISHED). Blank leaves their XP as it is'),
('rifts', 'gr_orb_count', 4.0, NULL, 'count', 'Greater Rift part 4 (card q-1006-02): progress orbs that appear when the last member of an elite pack dies in a Greater Rift. greater_rifts.csv rift_progress_elite_orbs: Champion/Rare packs in Greater Rifts always drop 4 purple progress orbs. Nephalem Rifts drop none (their orbs stay Phase C)'),
('rifts', 'gr_orb_display_id', NULL, 363.0, 'count', 'Greater Rift part 4 (card q-1006-02): the gameobject display of a progress orb, the stock purple arcane look (363 is the client''s ''Purple aura, short column'', gameobject_template 5622). Read by generate_rifts.py into rifts_0016_gr_orb.sql, so a change needs the generator rerun and that migration applied, not a .dc tunables set'),
('rifts', 'gr_orb_pickup_radius_yards', NULL, 5.5, 'yards', 'Greater Rift part 4 (card q-1006-02): how close a run member walks to an orb to take it. SEED, ALEX TUNES after he looks on dev: 5.5 is the core''s own INTERACTION_DISTANCE (ObjectDefines.h), the reach of every stock object pickup; D3 publishes no distance'),
('rifts', 'gr_orb_progress_pct', 1.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Greater Rift part 4 (card q-1006-02): the share of the whole progress bar one orb adds. greater_rifts.csv rift_progress_elite_orbs: 1% per orb'),
('rifts', 'gr_party_life_pct_per_extra_member', 100.0, NULL, 'percent', 'Greater Rift part 3: +this % of monster Life for each party member beyond the first, counted when the Greater Rift opens (later joiners do not count; the roster is closed anyway); monster damage unchanged. greater_rifts.csv multiplayer_life_scaling; party_scaling.csv greater_rift rows are 62.5/125/187.5/250%, which is the same +100% per member relative to the solo row (the 62.5% absolute base is not applied: the anchors, the brief and greater_rifts.csv all have solo at x1)'),
('rifts', 'gr_progress_weight_elite', 5.0, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 4 (diablocraft-del2; card q-1006-02, ruling 2026-10-06): progress a WoW elite-rank monster that is no pack member adds to the bar, as a multiple of one normal kill (a normal monster is x1, the Nephalem unit rifts/progress_units_per_kill). SEED, ALEX TUNES: greater_rifts.csv rift_progress_per_monster_type, Executioner 0.85% over 0.17% (the median of the ten published per-type examples, 0.04 0.09 0.09 0.12 0.15 0.19 0.23 0.38 0.46 0.85) = 5. Greater Rifts only; Nephalem Rifts count every kill as one'),
('rifts', 'gr_progress_weight_pack_member', 6.7647, NULL, 'multiplier', 'Greater Rift part 4 (card q-1006-02): progress each member of a promoted champion or rare pack (its leader too) adds to the bar, as a multiple of one normal kill. SEED, ALEX TUNES: greater_rifts.csv rift_progress_per_monster_type, an elite pack member 1.15% (blue pack 3.45%, yellow pack 4.60%) over the same 0.17% median = 6.7647. Greater Rifts only'),
('rifts', 'gr_proposal_timeout_seconds', NULL, 40.0, 'seconds', 'Greater Rift part 2 (diablocraft-0uyw; 09-rifts 7.9.2 item 2, the designer''s tunable seeded at 40 seconds, 2026-09-12): how long the party has to answer the Greater Rift ready check; the proposal waiting time is outside the 15:00 clock'),
('rifts', 'gr_revive_wait_first_seconds', 5.0, NULL, 'seconds', 'Greater Rift part 7 (diablocraft-214r), rule 5: the wait before a dead character may revive, after its first death in the run. greater_rifts.csv other_rules: respawn delay grows 5s to 30s per death'),
('rifts', 'gr_revive_wait_max_seconds', 30.0, NULL, 'seconds', 'Greater Rift part 7, rule 5: the wait never grows past this. greater_rifts.csv other_rules: respawn delay grows 5s to 30s per death'),
('rifts', 'gr_revive_wait_step_seconds', NULL, 5.0, 'seconds', 'Greater Rift part 7, rule 5: seconds added to the wait for every death after the first, up to gr_revive_wait_max_seconds. 5 since the designer, card q-1006-03 (docs/decisions.md 2026-10-06, diablocraft-tq4j): 5 s first, +5 per death, 30 s cap; greater_rifts.csv says only that the delay grows from 5s to 30s per death and publishes no step. Blank would mean no growth: every wait stays at gr_revive_wait_first_seconds'),
('rifts', 'gr_unlock_plus_10_min_seconds_left', 721.0, NULL, 'seconds', 'Greater Rift part 6 (diablocraft-hudw; docs/briefs/greater-rifts-brief.md part 6, ruling 2026-10-04; greater_rifts.csv keystone_upgrade_rule rows, bonus column corrected one row up): a Guardian killed with at least this many whole seconds left on the clock unlocks 10 levels above the beaten one; the row with the most seconds the kill reaches wins. The chart row is 12:01 or more remaining'),
